62: Central qualification discovery runs immediately after native lock acquisition in both `LockDataRoot`/`AcquireDataRootLease` and before returning the lock to ordinary callers. A distinct internal maintenance acquisition takes only the exact own-operation permit and still checks every other journal. This covers ordinary Core, coordinator's current raw LockDataRoot fallback, verifier replacement, inherited prepared recovery/migration native sessions, prepared-upgrade source lease and supervisor fixtures. No caller can suppress the check with an arbitrary string or boolean. The raw lock implementation is factored privately once to avoid acquisition recursion; existing callers preserve the normal checked API.
66: Fixture replay and backup CLI create/export currently reach store.Open outside normal Core startup. They must acquire/hold their exact DB-root lease and call combined gate before opening or reading credentials/Host setup. Fixture replay still enforces its original disposable fixture root. Backup upgrade paths already acquire source leases inside their domain workflow: add a callback-free qualification journal check there through the central checked lease and perform replacement history validation in the outer host-aware wrapper; if a workflow cannot hold its own source lease without double acquisition, freeze a borrowed-lease handoff in the implementation card and test it before acceptance, never drop the lease or silently skip the gate. Restore accepts only a new nonexisting destination; it must reject any alias to a live/pending data root and must not overwrite a journal. Read-only exported encrypted backup files outside the root have no pending-namespace bypass authority. store.Open additionally rejects an existing pending qualification namespace before its migration path; this is defense in depth, not a replacement for the entry's held lease.
