1: # B revision02 — first-gate rejection and closed FAILED qualification
3: DESIGN_ONLY; Source and actual authority NONE. Base Main `4f4023c956f84d65743f39ce77d6c8899a21ada1`, schema24. Requires accepted A candidate and serial ownership handoff of shared production files. This document addresses F06 and defines the real shared proof API consumed by D; C later adds a separately validated historical proof kind. Generic errors remain UNKNOWN. No migration, new launch, new public route or retrospective ACK is authorized.
7: `brokerEffect` decodes frame.Payload, calls dispatchGate, and calls providerRoute twice: first before prepareEffectTx, second after its transaction commits. Add the **only online constructor call at the first gate**, before the first providerRoute call. Do not upgrade generic errors inside providerRoute or qualificationModelEffectAllowed. The latter rejects TOOL before all binding checks; its generic error is insufficient evidence.
9: Private `qualificationPreEffectRejection` lives in `internal/domain/runtime_qualification_failure_windows.go`, with unexported fields and no JSON constructor. Constructor `qualificationFirstGateRejectionTx(tx, route, run, dispatch, frame, payload)` returns `(nil,nil)` when this narrow rule does not apply, typed rejection only for the exact validated case, and generic failure otherwise. It is invoked while the same first dispatchGate transaction holds resourceWriteLock, before any prepareEffectTx. Confirm dispatchGate's serialization in tests; if it lacks the write lock, take resourceWriteLock in this first-gate transaction before reading guards.
11: Required inputs are the current project/runtime/Task/Run/epoch/lease token and exact dispatch key+manifest hash; a real qualification Task and immutable plan; the matching runtime_qualification_runs marker and qualification admission; exact bound profile/technical hashes; frame type effect.request, capability TOOL, sequence3, valid Idempotency-Key, frozen route and payload digest. Verify the runtime route exists and matches project/runtime, qualification purpose, MODEL configuration route and frozen credential revision/upper bound; distinguish the known model route used in a prohibited TOOL request from an unknown route. Do not require a TOOL route to be granted: the fact being proved is that this validly bound qualification forbids TOOL. The payload must strictly match the supported TOOL request schema and captured raw frame; an invalid/malformed/unknown tool request is UNKNOWN. Require zero resource_effects history for the rejected key across all states, zero corresponding ledger reservation/event, and no prior dispatch of that key. Existing PREPARED/STARTED/CONFIRMED/NOT_APPLIED/UNKNOWN history denies typed construction. Second providerRoute call never invokes this constructor, even if the first stage is now denied.
13: The receipt binds schema `researchos.qualification-pre-effect-rejection.v1`, kind `ONLINE_FIRST_GATE_TOOL_DENIAL`, project/task/run/runtime/epoch, dispatch key+manifest hash, task and plan hashes, profile/technical hashes, frame sequence/type/capability/route/key, raw frame and canonical payload digests, stage `BEFORE_PREPARE_EFFECT_TX`, outcome `NO_EFFECT`, rule `QUALIFICATION_MODEL_ONLY_V1`, current observed_at, original sanitized first cause, and the zero-stage snapshot digest. No credentials, bearer values or private keys enter it. Create-new bounded immutable host file `qualification-rejection-00000000000000000003.json` under the exact dispatch directory, validate directory identity/private ACL/non-reparse ancestry, write and flush before propagating the typed error. Keep the transaction serialization until receipt persistence succeeds, then rollback the read-only transaction. Persistence failure returns ordinary UNKNOWN; a stray persisted receipt alone cannot close anything. Existing differing file is a conflict, not replacement. Exact same bytes may be read but terminal use still revalidates current facts.
19: On the first typed rejection, stop admitting new broker work, retain the original cause, cancel the dedicated broker context, cancel the bridge, and continue draining already submitted result completions and captured frames. Every launched goroutine must finish and join; all completion deliveries are consumed exactly once. No new frame is ACKed after the typed denial. Record any extra suffix/frame/stream activity as a disqualifier. Enforce bounded wait: timeout produces UNKNOWN and cannot yield a success/closed ticket; worker shutdown alone cannot replace this wait. No late goroutine may use a context that survives the fence. Generic error paths keep UNKNOWN but also cancel/join before leaving the scope where possible; if an external call cannot be proven ended, remain UNKNOWN. A private `qualificationBrokerDrain` ticket has no exported constructor and records accepted=completed, pending=0, admission closed and exact frame digests. The closure constructor requires this ticket, not a caller boolean.
25: The runtime adapter's new qualification_failure_proof_windows.go reads immutable bridge/native facts and provides bounded typed **input facts**, not an exported domain authorization. It validates captured stdout/stderr bytes, native identity and receipt, stopped children, streams drained, cleanup complete and outputs copied. Generic Bridge.Finalize and BridgeJournal.Observation retain their existing ACK equality rules.
27: Domain `verifyOnlineQualificationFailureTx` alone creates unexported `verifiedQualificationFailure`. It requires the typed denial + drained broker ticket + current exact dispatch/Run/Task/marker + native facts. Minimal v1: QueueRequired=false, no client queue rows or queue_control, no pause/resume/checkpoint state, exactly 3 captured frames, ACK2, one rejected sequence3, no suffix/holes/duplicates. Earlier MODEL effect is CONFIRMED and its request/receipt hashes match the acknowledged frame; all other effects are absent, including rejected TOOL key. No PREPARED, STARTED or UNKNOWN effect. An UNKNOWN monetary ledger with null money is preserved only for the confirmed MODEL under the already applicable accounting policy. Unknown effect outcome never qualifies.
29: Derived observation records FAILED, settled=false, frames3/acknowledged2/verified_rejected1, queue_empty=true only by this closed classification, raw bridge hash+sequence, rejection digest, drain census, and native cancellation/timed_out/exit facts. Never rewrite raw journal.State, frames, ACK, protocol_complete, artifacts, or native end time. Closure observed_at is distinct from native ended. The original cause and later causes remain separate.
31: `applyQualificationFailureTx(tx, verified, plannedFacts)` imports only a FAILED terminal fact, preserving old Task, active_run_id, qualification marker, consumed request, effects and all financial rows. It performs no reportRun/current execution permission bypass and no projectSessionRun for this non-queue qualification. The one transaction creates a separate GENERATED MANIFEST Artifact with run_id=null, actual authenticated Host scheduler principal as produced_by, its scoped project grant and current Owner-root binding in the envelope; this is not an old executor REPORT or a new member of native outputs. Existing original output artifacts remain unchanged. Use the same planned-artifact/event write rules as C, with kind ONLINE_FIRST_GATE_TOOL_DENIAL, and a stable marker operation `host:qualification-failure-closure`, key `run_id/epoch/denial_digest`. The marker binds proof Artifact VersionRef, observation digest, terminal Run revision/hash and outcome hash. Completed replay is zero-delta; conflicts fail closed. No budget release or NoProgress mutation is included.
39: func (c qualificationFailureClosure) proofRef() Object
43: The returned type has unexported fields; its zero value is rejected by consumers. The method loads the exact terminal Run, its matching qualification marker and plan, the matching immutable idempotency marker, Artifact version, sealed uploaded bytes and the runtime_observations row; recomputes all hashes; checks author/Owner-root binding and supported proof kind, subject identity, closed FAILED status, ACK/rejection counts, preserved raw source digests and terminal outcome binding. It does not accept an arbitrary provided proofRef, JSON boolean, injected callback, test registry or renderer status. No matching supported proof produces `QUALIFICATION_FAILURE_PROOF_UNAVAILABLE`. Mutable current-root revocation or changed binding rejects next-attempt admission without rewriting the historical proof.
45: B initially supports only ONLINE_FIRST_GATE_TOOL_DENIAL. C, after B acceptance and serial handoff, may extend the internal verifier to HISTORICAL_QUALIFICATION_NO_EFFECT_RECONSTRUCTION using C's independent historical checks and marker namespace. D calls this real method directly from its transaction before allocating a next attempt; D has no proof validator or constructor of its own. A/B source scope is not widened merely to make D fixtures pass. A legacy RUNNING/UNKNOWN run has no such proof and stays ineligible until separately accepted C executes.
49: Use existing domain/runtime native fixtures with temporary isolated roots. Validate known-route TOOL denial after one MODEL, invalid marker/route/key/payload/epoch, error persistence, unknown/suffix frames, second gate after PREPARED, pending/late provider goroutine, duplicated or lost completion, heartbeat race, native closure missing, corrupted source bytes, generic 503 and ordinary coding/tool behavior. Test full one-transaction rollback at each write and unchanged counters/ledger/ACK. No live provider or actual root is part of these tests. Architecture delivery has run no tests and grants no formal increment.
